# Gospel Presentation – Project Overview

## What this is
Next.js 16 app for "The Gospel in its Context" (Dr. Stuart Scott): counselor/counselee profiles, scripture modals (ESV/KJV/NASB/LSB), reflection questions, COMA method, print/share. Main app lives in **gospel-admin/**.

## Tech stack
- **Next.js 16** (App Router), **React 19**, **TypeScript**
- **Tailwind CSS 4** for styling
- **Supabase** (PostgreSQL, Auth, RLS)
- **Jest** + **React Testing Library** for tests
- **Capacitor** for iOS/Android (WebView of deployed site)

## Key paths
- `gospel-admin/src/app/` – App Router pages and API routes
- `gospel-admin/src/components/` – React components (e.g. ScriptureModal, GospelSection, ComaModal)
- `gospel-admin/src/lib/` – auth, Supabase, logger, data services
- `gospel-admin/sql/` – migrations and schema
- `docs/` – project documentation

## Conventions
- Use **logger** from `@/lib/logger` for server/API logging; avoid `console.log` in production paths.
- Sensitive config in env vars (Supabase, ESV API); never commit secrets.
- New UI must support **dark mode** (Tailwind `dark:` variants) to match existing components.
